## 2026-09-23 — Vercel – portfolio (ci-status.sh RED, head 221bf25)

Build error (Vercel build log, dpl_8DXTRhH6sspEmeQ19hycsAgiC7RF, bld_fn839d5ix):

    Error occurred prerendering page "/en/opengraph-image". Read more: https://nextjs.org/docs/messages/prerender-error
    Error: Only intrinsic elements are supported inside <svg>
    Error occurred prerendering page "/fr/opengraph-image" ...
    Error occurred prerendering page "/pt/opengraph-image" ...
    Export encountered an error on /[locale]/opengraph-image/route: /en/opengraph-image, exiting the build.
    Error: Command "pnpm run build" exited with 1

`websites/portfolio/app/[locale]/opengraph-image.tsx` renders `<LogoFull>`
(`packages/ui/src/components/brand/logo.tsx`), which rendered its shared frame markup through a
`Frame` custom component nested inside an `<svg>`. Satori (`next/og`'s SVG renderer) only resolves
intrinsic (lowercase) elements as direct descendants of `<svg>` — a custom component tag there is a
hard build error. This was silent on `next@16.2.9`; `next@16.3.6` bundles a stricter/different
Satori that enforces it.

- resolved: replaced the `Frame` component with a plain function `frame(ink)` returning an array of
  `<path>`/`<rect>` elements, called as `{frame(ink)}` (not `<Frame ink={ink} />`) at both call
  sites in `logo.tsx` — same markup, no custom element type in the tree.
- rule: nothing under `<svg>` in `@jamie-nisbet/ui`'s brand components (or anything rendered through
  `next/og`'s `ImageResponse`) may be a custom React component — Satori requires intrinsic elements
  only inside `<svg>`. Share sub-markup as a plain function returning an element array/fragment,
  called directly, never as a JSX component tag.
